@bank all
// CS1's words for 0.93.2's traditions (plans/trad-0932-words.txt and plans/tasting-table-late-words.md on
// claude/crew-stories-pitch 7b1e7300), pasted by FX24. Keys (section 18, the Traditions slot, behind TRAD_0932_ON):
//   t932.<id>.join    the host, when you tap them to join (one a day, by the day)
//   t932.<id>.close   the host, near the end (a bubble, once)
//   tasting.dish.<key>  Brennan's dishes, "name | what she says setting it down"; two a week in turn (the keys: the tally's choices)
//   tasting.greet / tasting.ask / tasting.thanks / tasting.close   Brennan when you join the tasting table

// scone-morning (host halloran-emeka)
== t932.scone-morning.join
- Morning! Scone? Joke first or scone first? Scone first. I'm not a monster.
- There you are. Warm one, from the middle of the tin. Best ones.
- Sit, sit. Jam's there. Here's today's joke, you've been warned.
== t932.scone-morning.close
- That's the tin empty. Lovely. Same again in a few weeks.
- Last scone's yours. And the last joke. Sorry about the joke.

// rec-ring-the-bell (host chen-carmen)
== t932.rec-ring-the-bell.join
- Oh. You're climbing? Good. Chalk's there. The bell's waiting.
- One climb, the hard route. Don't look down. Well, look a bit.
- You're next. Everyone counts. It helps. It doesn't help.
== t932.rec-ring-the-bell.close
- That's everyone. The bell's still ringing in my ears. Or it isn't. Hard to say.
- Next month, then. The bell isn't going anywhere.

// coffee-trials (host volkov-maeve)
== t932.coffee-trials.join
- Hiya! Three cups. No names. Taste, then vote. Cup B is not mine. Probably.
- Here, sip. Don't say anything yet. Faces only.
- You're a judge now. Very serious job. Have a biscuit.
== t932.coffee-trials.close
- Tokens are in. And the winner is... the coffee machine, honestly. Ta-ra!
- That's the trials. Nobody tell Calder we used the machine three times.

// five-minute-skills (host nakamura-bilal)
== t932.five-minute-skills.join
- Good, you came. Sit there. Five minutes, I'm timing it.
- Today's skill is a small one. Small skills save big days.
- Watch first. Then your hands. Then mine, if yours get stuck.
== t932.five-minute-skills.close
- Five minutes. Well, eight. Everyone's got it. Mostly.
- That's one more thing you know. Come back for the next one.

// beginners-guitar (host larsen-hamid)
== t932.beginners-guitar.join
- You came! Brave. Sit near the door, in case.
- Right, you're our audience. Clap whatever happens.
- Here's the guitar. One chord. G. Ish.
== t932.beginners-guitar.close
- That's our set. All three songs. Two of them were the same song.
- Thanks for listening. Your ears will recover.

// windowsill-herbs (host janssen-hugo)
== t932.windowsill-herbs.join
- Hello! Smell this one. No, closer. That's the good basil.
- Brought a pot? Lovely. No pot? Have a cutting.
- We're judging the parsley today. Gently. It's sensitive.
== t932.windowsill-herbs.close
- Best bunch goes to Brennan. Everyone else takes a cutting home.
- That's the herbs swapped. The garden smells amazing now.

// sounds-from-home (host vasquez-uma)
== t932.sounds-from-home.join
- Hi. Sit anywhere. We're about to play a harbour. Then someone's grandad's clock.
- Have you brought a sound? If not, just listen. That's half of it.
- Lights low. Ears open. That's all we need.
== t932.sounds-from-home.close
- That's everyone's. Thank you for bringing a bit of home aboard.
- Same time next month. Bring a different sound. Or the same one, if you miss it.

// jar-day (host varga-tariq)
== t932.jar-day.join
- Apron's on the hook. Jars are washed. Beans are waiting.
- You fill, I seal, you label. Neat letters, please.
- Today it's carrots. Last time it was a sort of jam. We don't talk about it.
== t932.jar-day.close
- Forty jars. Forty-one. Who brought an extra jar? Never mind. Shelf it.
- That's jar day. Your name's on the spice shelf now.

// rec-lamplight-paddle (host silva-bea)
== t932.rec-lamplight-paddle.join
- Hello. Grab a paddle. No racing. I mean it.
- Slow is the only speed tonight.
- Sit low, paddle soft. The lamps do the rest.
== t932.rec-lamplight-paddle.close
- That's the river done. Out slowly, and mind the dock board.
- Thank you for drifting with me. Sleep well tonight. You will.

// playlist-duel (host oneill-imani)
== t932.playlist-duel.join
- You came! Pick a side. Left plays first.
- Three songs each. Vote with your hands. I'll count. Honestly.
- No skipping, no booing. Clapping's fine.
== t932.playlist-duel.close
- Left wins. I let them. Obviously.
- Duel's done. Somebody's playlist goes on the jam's list on Friday.

// row-for-the-board (host lindqvist-isak)
== t932.row-for-the-board.join
- You're here to shout? Good. Loud's what I need.
- Two minutes each. Vance's name is up there. Not for long.
- Count the metres out loud. Every hundred. Please.
== t932.row-for-the-board.close
- Not tonight. Close, though. Next month.
- The board stays as it is. For now. Write that down.

// seed-packet-day (host hart-ravi)
== t932.seed-packet-day.join
- Hello. Paper, seeds, pencils. Fold first. Draw after.
- Pick your seeds from the jars. Then make the packet look like them.
- Your drawing goes in Cruz's tin. For a whole season.
== t932.seed-packet-day.close
- That's the packets done. Cruz will sow them next season. Your names and all.
- Thank you. That's next season sorted.

// midnight-toast (host garcia-greta)
== t932.midnight-toast.join
- Still up? Fine. Sit. Toast's coming.
- This is for the night shift. You can have some. Don't tell them.
- Butter or jam? Wrong. Both.
== t932.midnight-toast.close
- Night shift's off to work. Go to bed, owls.
- Last slice gone. Kitchen's closing. Sleep.

// whodunnit-club (host achterberg-lars)
== t932.whodunnit-club.join
- Pencil, paper. Sit. Part one starts in a minute.
- No guessing out loud. Write it down. Fold it over.
- Tonight's is short. The culprit isn't.
== t932.whodunnit-club.close
- And it was... the one nobody wrote down. As usual.
- That's the mystery. Same time next month. Bring suspicions.

// Brennan's tasting table (after dinner, the galley)
== tasting.dish.smoked-salt-caramels
- Smoked salt caramels | Marra Station salt. Bite first, then tell me.
== tasting.dish.seaweed-crackers
- Seaweed crackers | Off the hydroponics wall. Crunchy. You'll see.
== tasting.dish.lentil-dumplings
- Spiced lentil dumplings | My mum's, by ear. Until it sounds right.
== tasting.dish.green-tomato-oatcakes
- Green tomato chutney on oatcakes | The garden was too keen. This is the fix.
== tasting.dish.cardamom-rice-pudding
- Cardamom rice pudding | Kovac sorted the pods. Every one.
== tasting.dish.chilli-lime-popcorn
- Chilli-lime popcorn | Nandakumar's chillies. Have water ready.
== tasting.dish.cold-beetroot-soup
- Cold beetroot soup | Cold soup. Don't make that face.
== tasting.dish.thyme-honey-flatbread
- Honey and thyme flatbread | Hugo's thyme. He'll want a report.
== tasting.dish.black-bean-fritters
- Black bean fritters | Crisp outside. Hold it by the edge, love.
== tasting.dish.mushroom-broth-cup
- Mushroom broth in a cup | Drink it. It's soup you hold.
== tasting.dish.pear-ginger-crumble
- Pear and ginger crumble | Pears from the stores. Ginger for the cold.
== tasting.dish.pickled-carrot-ribbons
- Pickled carrot ribbons | From jar day. Tariq's jar, not yours.
== tasting.dish.sesame-noodle-nest
- Sesame noodle nests | Twirl, don't slurp. Well. Slurp a bit.
== tasting.dish.baked-plum-custard
- Baked plum custard | Wobbles when it's right. Look at it wobble.
== tasting.dish.herb-omelette-roll
- Rolled herb omelette | Breakfast, but after dark. Live a little.
== tasting.dish.sweet-potato-cakes
- Sweet potato cakes | Mashed by Lukas. Fried by me. Blame him.
== tasting.greet
- Come through, love. Spoon's there. Two new ones tonight.
- There you are. Clean spoon, open mind. Try the left one first.
- Sit on the stool. Taste both before you say a word.
== tasting.ask
- Right. Which jar gets your token? Don't be polite.
- Left jar or right jar, love. Honest answer.
- Token in a jar, please. I won't look. I'll look a bit.
== tasting.thanks
- Thank you, love. If it wins, it's on Sunday's table.
- Noted. You've got taste. Or you've got mine, anyway.
- Lovely. Off you go, and take a biscuit for the road.
== tasting.close
- That's tonight's. Back out, the lot of you, I've pans to do.
- Thank you, loves. The winner's on Sunday. The loser never happened.
